course: dictionary
lesson: 14921
title: A word with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Refreshments usually means small amounts of food and drink, like the snacks at a school fair. «Refreshments will be served in the hall after the concert.» The words around it (served, hall, concert) show you the food-and-drink meaning.
explain: Look at the clues around the word to choose the right meaning. «The walkers stopped at the top of the hill for refreshments.» Walkers, stopped and hill make you think of a snack and a drink on a journey. Always check: does my meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Grown-ups sometimes use refreshments as a polite, jokey way to talk about alcoholic drinks. «The sign said: Liquid refreshments available at the bar.» Liquid refreshment almost always hints at beer or wine, so this is the grown-up meaning, not a snack. If you are not sure, ask a grown-up.
explain: There is a third, more formal meaning: the feeling of being refreshed. «The cool breeze was a welcome refreshment after the hot climb.» Here refreshment is singular, and it means feeling fresh and full of energy again.
fact: Refreshments means small amounts of food and drink offered at a meeting, event or journey.
fact: Refreshments is a plural noun; the singular refreshment can mean the feeling of being refreshed.
fact: Refreshments can be a euphemism: a polite, jokey way of saying alcoholic drinks.
fact: «Liquid refreshments» almost always hints at beer or wine.
fact: To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Refreshments will be served in the hall after the concert.» What are refreshments here? | A school uniform rule | *Small amounts of food and drink served at an event | Tools for cleaning the hall | A kind of music
exercise: «The sign said: Liquid refreshments available at the bar.» What does this hint at? | Sandwiches and cake | *Alcoholic drinks, like beer or wine | Hot soup for the winter | Fruit juice and water
exercise: «The cool breeze was a welcome refreshment after the hot climb.» What does refreshment mean here? | A plate of cakes | A cold, wet day | *The feeling of being fresh and full of energy again | A cup of tea served at a shop
test: «Please help yourself to refreshments at the back of the room.» Which word is the singular form of refreshments? | refreshers | refreshing | *refreshment | refreshed
test: Mia says refreshments always means snacks. What is the best reply? | It means a tired, sleepy feeling | *Not always, since it can also be a polite word for alcoholic drinks | It is the name of a football match | Yes, it always means snacks and nothing else
exam: «The walkers stopped for refreshments at the top of the hill.» Which meaning fits best? | The name of a hill | A loud noise | *Small amounts of food and drink, taken on a journey | A kind of tent
